[Audio:random-noise:Random Noise]
Played by #R$A70D and #R$A713, when the entity is visible.
The pitches come from random places in the ROM, so this is one example.

#AUDIO0(random-noise.wav)(#INCLUDE(RandomNoise))

[Audio:appearing-sound:Appearing Sound]
Played by #R$A940 and #R$A965.
The pitch is random, so this is one example.

#AUDIO0(appearing-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(AppearingSound))

[Audio:action-sound:Action Sound]
Started by #R$AC96 when the action key is used. Four tones.
#R$BFDA does not read the effect number. Each tone's pitch list is chosen
from #REGa' at that frame. This is the sound at the start of play, when the
first tone's #REGa' is #N$50.

#AUDIO0(action-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ActionSound))

[Audio:program-sent-sound:Program Sent Sound]
Started by #R$9E45 when a program packet is sent. Five tones.
The pitch list is chosen from #REGa', not from effect number #N$01. This is
the sound at the start of play.

#AUDIO0(program-sent-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ProgramSentSound))

[Audio:sector-activated-sound:Sector Activated Sound]
Started by #R$A440 when a sector is activated. Seven tones.
The pitch list is chosen from #REGa', not from effect number #N$02. This is
the sound at the start of play.

#AUDIO0(sector-activated-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(SectorActivatedSound))

[Audio:program-destroyed-sound:Program Destroyed Sound]
Started by #R$A3F4 when a program is destroyed. Four tones.
Effect #N$00 is also four tones and the effect number is not read, so this
is the same sound as the action sound. This is it at the start of play.

#AUDIO0(program-destroyed-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ProgramDestroyedSound))
